<title>NEW ZEALAND: BNZ lowers NZ 2 and 3 yr fixed rates to 9.9 pct.</title>
<headline>BNZ lowers NZ 2 and 3 yr fixed rates to 9.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of New Zealand said on Wednesday it had lowered its two and three-year fixed home lending rate to 9.9 percent from 10.5 percent.  </p>
<p>Bank of New Zealand managing director Gordon Wheaton said the interest rate reduction was part of the bank's policy of passing on benefits of lower funding costs to customers.</p>
<p>Business and farming fixed lending rates were left unchanged although under review.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
